  "observations": [
    "Directly viewed 20 close poses in four directions: brown headcloth, short beard, yellow natural chest hair in front, strong torso, grey trousers/sash and bare feet retain Ruan Xiaoer. Both hands meet handles; selected push name/HP clear the silhouette. No obvious opaque box or neighbour-frame bleed at sampled close/default/1.6 views, including narrow passing-A gutter.",
    "Actual four-direction movement images retain own cart; native probe traverses four frame indices. Front B/crossing phase visibly changes foot position after the rejected first source. Rear B/passing-B foot silhouettes remain similar and cadence/opposite support could be more natural; do not claim final gait realism. Cart cloth, rope, wheel-spoke and some body silhouette continuity remain polish.",
    "Eight hurt/attack views use the original Ruan body beside a parked independent cart. Old hurt/attack name/HP and weapons still approach or partly cover the head area; enemy tags overlap. Those old UI issues remain open.",
    "Original pickup and defeat/drop are crowded by escort shoulder-art, enemy names and floating damage. Delivery correctly restores own original body/portrait beside the ground cart; four locale portraits remain correct, but mixed goods/messages and three-target/shoulder wording remain.",
    "Twenty actual startup-camera poses, four 1.6 passing-B views and actual delivery-unloaded default view were inspected. Default SE screenshots retain temporary 22 damage text near the name. FPS includes capture/freeze effects, not a performance result.",
    "This is an unchanged full base PCK plus a real exported 8046408-byte patch, with frozen external QA loading mounted production resources. It is not a new monolithic full PCK, complete natural wine-plot playthrough, seven-cart/eleven-burden migration, whole UI/localization, save/campaign/performance, Steam or all-art acceptance."
  ]
